{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790256667,"nonce":"0ypZaKfu7EZWKop+jTsV42Y9e7Q=","message":"Partly addressed by 7fe5fe27 (package l2): debug.setmetatable and debug.getmetatable are now typed as setmetatable and getmetatable, so the classes they give or expose are tracked. The absent_field_ty half is still open. Passing the class's __index (not the class) to index_chain_ty is the right chain, but it makes method_call 18x slower: NthToggle.new is not born in NthToggle, so its read joins NthToggle.new with Toggle.new (behind the __index), two different Funcs join to Any, NthToggle.new(...) becomes a dynamic call and every method escapes. The fix needs the join of the own field with what lies behind it to keep a set of functions (or trust a field that every path through the program has stored before the read) rather than going to Any.","files":null}]}